<div class="bb-quote"><b>Ameena wrote:</b><br /><blockquote class="bb-quote-body">Am I the only one around here who doesn&#39;t even know what poutine is? Mind you, my idea of cooking is &quot;bung it in the microwave, wait the required number of minutes, then take it out, peel the lid off, and eat it&quot;, so...
&nbsp;
</blockquote></div>
That&#39;s how my boyfriend &quot;cooks&quot;. He has no interest in doing anything more elaborate. Best he can do is a cheese omelette.Needless to say, I&#39;m the one in charge of food preparation in our house. I&#39;m always horrified by how much unnecessary salt and sugar they have to put into ready meals to make them even half palatable, and besides I actually really like following recipes and creating my own dishes.

[/quote]

&nbsp;

Funnily enough, I used to work for a company that were the largest supplier of ready meals in the UK. I had a visit to one of the factories and was amazed at all the beautiful fresh vegetables and herbs, thousands of trays of the stuff in every part of the building, and every room was filled with the most incredible aromas. And then I looked at the crappy processed end product pumped full of all the bad things and made a little sad face.
